e4all for Horizon
=================

This is an unofficial port. It is not e4all, and it is not made or endorsed
by the e4all project or its authors.

What it is built on:

  e4all — the Java mod this ports.
    Copyright (c) the e4all authors. MIT.
    https://github.com/Synquox/e4all
    e4all is a fork of e4mc.

  e4mc — the mod whose relay protocol this speaks, and whose Java client the
  Rust client here is a port of.
    Copyright (c) vgskye and contributors. MIT.
    https://github.com/vgskye/e4mc-minecraft-architectury

  e4mc-quiclime — the relay's server side, which defines the wire format this
  mod speaks (the control messages and their framing).
    Copyright (c) vgskye. MIT OR Apache-2.0.
    https://github.com/vgskye/e4mc-quiclime

  Horizon — the game this mod runs in, and horizon-mixins, the tool that
  builds native mods for it.
    Copyright (c) the Horizon authors. MIT.
    https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon
    https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon-mixins

The relay's own service (the domains, the broker and the relays) is run by
the e4mc project; this mod is only a client of it.

